# name, family, color, ref(full), drQuote, refShort, L1 meaning, L2 meaning, keyLine, m1, m2, talk1, talk2, prayer, cardText, words
V = [
("Creativity","Wisdom","gold","Genesis 1:31","And God saw all the things that he had made, and they were very good.","Gn 1:31",
 "Creativity means thinking up new ideas and using them for good. God made the whole world, and He gave you an imagination too!",
 "Creativity is the gift of finding new and helpful ways to do things. God is the first Creator: He made the stars, the seas, and you. When we invent, draw, build, or solve a problem in a fresh way, and use that idea to help others or give glory to God, we share in His creative work. A creative idea is best when it is also a good idea.",
 "God made me to make good things.",
 ["Draw a picture of something God made","Build something new with blocks or boxes","Make up a kind song for your family","Find a new way to help with a chore","Make a thank-you card for someone","Create a small prayer corner at home"],
 ["Solve a family problem in a brand-new way","Design a card to cheer up someone sad","Write a short story that teaches a virtue","Reuse something old to make something useful","Plan a creative surprise for a family member","Make an art gift for Jesus or Mary"],
 ["What new idea did someone in our family have this week?","How did our ideas help other people?"],
 "Dear God, Creator of all, help me use my ideas to make good and beautiful things. Amen.",
 "God made the world very good, and He gave me ideas to make good things too!", ["create","idea","imagine","make"]),
("Curiosity","Wisdom","gold","Matthew 7:7","Seek, and you shall find: knock, and it shall be opened to you.","Mt 7:7",
 "Curiosity means being interested in new things and wanting to explore. God's world is full of wonders waiting to be found!",
 "Curiosity is a holy wondering. It means asking good questions, noticing new things, and wanting to explore God's world. Jesus told us to seek and knock. A curious heart wants to learn about plants, animals, people, and most of all about God. Curiosity grows when we ask, look closely, and listen for answers.",
 "I will seek and find.",
 ["Ask a grown-up one 'why' question","Look closely at a bug, leaf, or cloud","Ask Grandma or Grandpa about their childhood","Learn the name of a new animal","Ask a question about Jesus at dinner","Explore a new place in your yard or park"],
 ["Look up the answer to a question you wonder about","Learn three facts about a saint","Ask a family member about their work","Find out how something at home works","Read about a country you have never visited","Ask a priest or catechist a faith question"],
 ["What was the most interesting thing we discovered this week?","What do we still wonder about God's world?"],
 "Jesus, fill me with wonder. Help me seek You in everything I learn. Amen.",
 "Jesus said, \"Seek, and you shall find.\" A curious heart loves to explore God's world.", ["seek","wonder","explore","ask"]),
("Open-Mindedness","Wisdom","gold","James 1:19","Let every man be swift to hear, but slow to speak.","Jas 1:19",
 "Open-mindedness means looking at things from every fair side before deciding. We listen first, then we choose.",
 "Open-mindedness means thinking about a situation from every fair side before we make up our minds. We do not jump to conclusions. We listen to other people, look at the facts, and are willing to change our minds when we learn something true. Saint James says to be quick to hear and slow to speak. An open mind still holds tight to God's truth, while listening with love.",
 "I listen first, then I decide.",
 ["Listen to a friend's idea all the way through","Try a food you think you won't like","Play a game your sibling chooses","Ask, 'What do you think?' to someone","Say 'Maybe you're right' once today","Pray before making a choice"],
 ["Hear both sides before settling an argument","Ask someone why they think differently","Change your mind when you learn something true","Read about a saint very different from you","Look for facts before judging a story","Ask the Holy Spirit to help you think fairly"],
 ["When did we listen before deciding this week?","Did anyone change their mind after learning something new?"],
 "Holy Spirit, open my ears and my mind. Help me listen and think fairly. Amen.",
 "Be quick to listen and slow to speak. Look at every fair side before deciding.", ["listen","fair","think","open"]),
("Love of Learning","Wisdom","gold","Proverbs 1:5","A wise man shall hear, and shall be wiser.","Prv 1:5",
 "Love of learning means wanting to learn new skills and new things. Every day God gives us a chance to grow!",
 "Love of learning is the joy of growing in skills and knowledge. It means practicing until we master something new, reading, asking, and trying again. God gave us minds to know Him and His world. Saints like Thomas Aquinas loved to learn so they could love God more. Learning is not just for school; it is a lifelong adventure with Jesus.",
 "I love to learn and grow.",
 ["Learn a new word and use it today","Practice reading for ten minutes","Learn one line of a new prayer","Ask someone to teach you a skill","Learn a fact about a saint","Show your family something you learned"],
 ["Set one learning goal for the week","Practice a hard skill for 15 minutes","Memorize a short Bible verse","Teach a younger child something you know","Read a chapter of a good book","Learn more about one part of the Mass"],
 ["What new thing did each of us learn this week?","What would we like to learn together next?"],
 "Lord, thank You for my mind. Help me learn with joy and grow wiser each day. Amen.",
 "A wise person listens and becomes wiser. God loves when we learn and grow!", ["learn","grow","read","practice"]),
("Perspective","Wisdom","gold","James 1:5","If any of you want wisdom, let him ask of God, who giveth to all men abundantly.","Jas 1:5",
 "Perspective means seeing the big picture and making wise choices. We can ask God for wisdom anytime!",
 "Perspective is a wise way of seeing the world and making important decisions. It means stepping back to see the big picture, thinking about what matters most, and giving good advice. People with perspective remember that God's plan is bigger than one bad day. Saint James says that if we need wisdom, we should ask God, who gives generously.",
 "God, help me see the big picture.",
 ["Ask God for wisdom when you wake up","Think: Will this matter tomorrow?","Ask a parent for advice on a choice","Give a friend kind, helpful advice","Remember a hard day that turned out fine","Thank God for His big, good plan"],
 ["Before a big choice, list the good and bad","Ask an elder what they learned in life","Calm a small problem by seeing the big picture","Give honest advice when someone asks","Think about what Jesus would choose","Pray for wisdom for our family"],
 ["What helped us see the big picture this week?","What good advice did someone give us?"],
 "Lord, give me wisdom. Help me see what matters most and choose what is good. Amen.",
 "If you need wisdom, ask God! He gives it generously.", ["wisdom","advice","choose","plan"]),
("Courage","Courage","red","Joshua 1:9","Take courage, and be strong. Fear not... because the Lord thy God is with thee.","Jos 1:9",
 "Courage means doing and saying what is right, even when it is hard or scary. God is always with you!",
 "Courage, or bravery, means speaking and acting for what is right even when it is hard or scary. Brave people still feel afraid, but they trust God and do the right thing anyway. God told Joshua to be strong and not to fear, because He would be with him everywhere he went. Martyrs and saints show us that real courage comes from loving God more than we fear.",
 "God is with me. I can be brave.",
 ["Try something new even if you feel shy","Say sorry first after an argument","Stand up for someone left out","Pray when you feel afraid","Raise your hand to answer at school","Tell the truth even when it is hard"],
 ["Speak up kindly when something is wrong","Invite someone sitting alone to join you","Say no to something you know is wrong","Make the Sign of the Cross before eating out","Face one fear with a parent's help","Pray for people who are persecuted"],
 ["When was someone in our family brave this week?","What helps us feel brave when we are afraid?"],
 "Jesus, You are with me always. Give me courage to do what is right. Amen.",
 "\"Take courage, and be strong. Fear not.\" God is with me wherever I go.", ["brave","strong","courage","fear"]),
("Perseverance","Courage","red","Galatians 6:9","And in doing good, let us not fail. For in due time we shall reap, not failing.","Gal 6:9",
 "Perseverance means finishing what you start, even when it is hard. Don't give up!",
 "Perseverance means sticking with a good task until it is finished. It means keeping on when things are slow, boring, or difficult. Saint Paul says not to grow tired of doing good, because in time we will see the harvest. Jesus kept going all the way to the cross for love of us. With God's help, we can keep trying.",
 "I will not give up.",
 ["Finish one task before starting another","Try again after a mistake","Finish all of your homework","Keep practicing a hard skill","Clean up your toys all the way","Finish your prayers without rushing"],
 ["Work on a big project a little each day","Finish a book you started","Keep a promise you made","Try a hard problem three times before asking","Stick with a chore until it is done well","Pray a whole decade of the Rosary"],
 ["What did we finish this week that was hard?","How did we encourage each other to keep going?"],
 "Lord Jesus, when things are hard, help me keep going and never give up on doing good. Amen.",
 "Do not get tired of doing good. Keep going, and you will see the harvest!", ["finish","try","persevere","patient"]),
("Honesty","Courage","red","Ephesians 4:25","Wherefore putting away lying, speak ye the truth every man with his neighbour.","Eph 4:25",
 "Honesty means telling the truth and acting the same way when no one is watching. Jesus is the Truth!",
 "Honesty means telling the truth and living with integrity: being the same person on the inside and the outside. Honest people keep promises, admit mistakes, and do not cheat or take what is not theirs. Saint Paul tells us to put away lying and speak the truth. Jesus said, \"I am the way, and the truth, and the life.\" When we are honest, we follow Him.",
 "I will tell the truth.",
 ["Tell the truth about something you did","Keep a promise you made","Return something that isn't yours","Admit a mistake and say sorry","Play a game fairly without cheating","Tell God the truth in your prayers"],
 ["Own up to a mistake before someone asks","Be honest even when it costs you","Give back extra change or credit","Keep your word on a chore you promised","Do your work honestly, without copying","Prepare for an honest Confession"],
 ["When was telling the truth hard this week?","How does honesty help our family trust each other?"],
 "Jesus, You are the Truth. Help me speak truthfully and keep my promises. Amen.",
 "Put away lying and speak the truth. Jesus is the Truth!", ["truth","honest","promise","trust"]),
("Zest","Courage","red","Psalm 118:24","This is the day which the Lord hath made: let us be glad and rejoice therein.","Ps 118:24",
 "Zest means living with energy and joy. Each day is a gift from God to enjoy!",
 "Zest means living with energy, excitement, and interest. People with zest wake up ready for the day and put their whole heart into what they do. They do not do things halfway. The psalm says that this is the day the Lord has made, so let us be glad! Zest comes from knowing that every day is a gift from God to use well.",
 "This is the day the Lord has made!",
 ["Wake up and say, 'Good morning, God!'","Play outside with all your energy","Help with a chore cheerfully","Sing a happy song to Jesus","Do something fun as a family","Try your best at something new"],
 ["Start the day with a morning offering","Get exercise or play a sport","Do a task with your whole heart","Get enough sleep to be ready for tomorrow","Share your excitement with someone","Plan a joyful family activity for Sunday"],
 ["What made us excited and full of energy this week?","How can we enjoy each day as God's gift?"],
 "Lord, thank You for this new day. Help me live it with joy and energy for You. Amen.",
 "This is the day the Lord has made. Let us be glad and rejoice!", ["joy","energy","glad","today"]),
("Love","Humanity","red","John 13:34","A new commandment I give unto you: That you love one another, as I have loved you.","Jn 13:34",
 "Love means caring for the people close to us, like family and friends. Jesus loves us first!",
 "Love means valuing close relationships, where we give and receive care. It is shown in hugs, kind words, time together, and sacrifices for each other. Jesus gave us a new commandment: love one another as I have loved you. Our families are the first place we learn to love, and God's love is the source of all love.",
 "I love because Jesus loves me.",
 ["Give a family member a big hug","Say 'I love you' to someone","Spend time with a brother or sister","Draw a picture for someone you love","Pray for each person in your family","Help a parent without being asked"],
 ["Spend screen-free time with your family","Write a note telling someone why you love them","Call or visit a grandparent","Do a family member's chore for them","Listen to someone's whole day","Pray together as a family tonight"],
 ["How did we show love to each other this week?","Who outside our home can we love better?"],
 "Jesus, You loved me first. Help me love my family and friends as You love me. Amen.",
 "Jesus said, \"Love one another, as I have loved you.\"", ["love","family","care","friend"]),
("Kindness","Humanity","red","Acts 20:35","It is a more blessed thing to give, rather than to receive.","Acts 20:35",
 "Kindness means doing good and helping people. A kind heart is generous and loves to share!",
 "Kindness means doing good things for others, helping them, and caring for them. A kind heart is also a generous heart: it shares toys, time, and treats without expecting anything back. Jesus said it is more blessed to give than to receive. Every kind act, big or small, is a way of loving Jesus, who said that what we do for others we do for Him.",
 "It is better to give than to receive.",
 ["Share a toy or snack with someone","Help someone who needs a hand","Say something kind to a classmate","Give a smile to everyone you meet","Make a gift for someone",
  "Put a coin in the poor box at church"],
 ["Do a secret kind deed for a family member","Give away a toy or book in good shape","Help a neighbor with a small job","Include someone who is often left out","Write a kind note to a teacher","Save money to give to people in need"],
 ["What kind or generous thing did we see this week?","What can our family share with others?"],
 "Jesus, make my heart kind and generous. Help me give with joy, like You. Amen.",
 "It is more blessed to give than to receive. A kind heart loves to share.", ["kind","share","give","help"]),
("Social Intelligence","Humanity","red","Romans 12:15","Rejoice with them that rejoice; weep with them that weep.","Rom 12:15",
 "Social intelligence means noticing how others feel and choosing the right words and actions.",
 "Social intelligence means noticing other people's feelings and knowing what to say and do. It helps us know when a friend needs a hug, a joke, quiet time, or help. Saint Paul says to rejoice with those who rejoice and weep with those who weep. Jesus always noticed people: the lonely, the sick, and the sad. We can learn to notice too.",
 "I notice how others feel.",
 ["Notice when someone looks sad","Ask, 'How are you feeling today?'","Celebrate a friend's good news","Use a gentle voice with someone upset","Wait your turn to talk","Thank someone and look them in the eye"],
 ["Read someone's face and respond kindly","Comfort a friend who is having a hard day","Choose kind words when you disagree","Notice who needs a turn and give it","Help two friends make peace","Pray for someone you noticed was hurting"],
 ["When did we notice someone's feelings this week?","What words help someone who is sad or upset?"],
 "Jesus, You saw every person's heart. Help me notice others and care for them. Amen.",
 "Rejoice with those who rejoice; weep with those who weep.", ["feelings","notice","gentle","friend"]),
("Citizenship","Justice","green","Galatians 6:2","Bear ye one another's burdens; and so you shall fulfil the law of Christ.","Gal 6:2",
 "Citizenship means working together and doing your part for your family, class, parish, and town.",
 "Citizenship means cooperating with others, being loyal to the groups we belong to, and doing our part. We are members of a family, a class, a parish, a town, and a country. Each one needs us! Saint Paul says to carry one another's burdens. Good citizens help the team, follow fair rules, care for shared places, and serve the common good.",
 "I will do my part.",
 ["Do your chores without being asked","Clean up a mess you didn't make","Follow the rules at school","Help your team in a game","Pick up litter at the park","Help get ready for Mass on Sunday"],
 ["Join a parish service project","Help a classmate on a group project","Care for something shared, like a park","Pray for leaders of our country","Recycle and take care of creation","Thank a firefighter, nurse, or helper"],
 ["How did each of us do our part this week?","How can our family help our parish or town?"],
 "Lord, help me be a good member of my family, parish, and town. Help me do my part. Amen.",
 "Carry one another's burdens. Every member of the team matters!", ["team","help","serve","community"]),
("Fairness","Justice","green","Matthew 7:12","All things therefore whatsoever you would that men should do to you, do you also to them.","Mt 7:12",
 "Fairness means treating everyone the same good way, not just the people we like.",
 "Fairness means treating everyone justly and equally, not deciding things only by our private feelings. A fair person gives everyone a turn, follows the rules, and does not play favorites. Jesus gave us the Golden Rule: treat others the way you want to be treated. Every person is made in God's image, so every person deserves to be treated fairly.",
 "I treat others the way I want to be treated.",
 ["Take turns in a game","Share treats equally","Let someone else go first","Play with someone you don't usually play with","Follow the rules even when losing","Listen to both sides of a story"],
 ["Divide a task fairly with a sibling","Include everyone in a group game","Be fair to someone you don't like","Admit when the other side is right","Stand up for someone treated unfairly","Pray for people who suffer injustice"],
 ["When did we treat someone fairly this week?","How can we include everyone at school or church?"],
 "Jesus, help me treat everyone fairly, the way I want to be treated. Amen.",
 "Treat others the way you want them to treat you: the Golden Rule.", ["fair","turns","rule","equal"]),
("Leadership","Justice","green","Mark 10:43","Whosoever will be greater, shall be your minister.","Mk 10:43",
 "Leadership means helping a group reach a goal while helping everyone get along. Leaders serve!",
 "Leadership means guiding a group toward a good goal while helping everyone get along. A Christian leader is a servant leader. Jesus said that whoever wants to be great must serve the others, and He washed His disciples' feet. Good leaders listen, encourage, plan, and make sure no one is left out. You can lead at home, at school, and at church.",
 "A leader serves.",
 ["Help a younger child learn something","Lead your family in grace before meals","Invite others to play and include all","Encourage a teammate who is trying","Lead a family clean-up time","Help plan a fun family activity"],
 ["Lead a family prayer or Bible reading","Organize a game where everyone fits in","Help a group solve a problem calmly","Set a good example for younger kids","Listen to everyone's ideas before deciding","Serve someone like Jesus washing feet"],
 ["When did someone in our family lead by serving?","How can we lead others toward Jesus?"],
 "Jesus, You came to serve. Help me lead others with kindness and help everyone get along. Amen.",
 "Whoever wants to be great must serve. Leaders serve like Jesus!", ["lead","serve","guide","team"]),
("Forgiveness","Temperance","white","Ephesians 4:32","Be ye kind one to another; merciful, forgiving one another, even as God hath forgiven you in Christ.","Eph 4:32",
 "Forgiveness means letting go of hurt and giving people a second chance, just as God forgives us.",
 "Forgiveness and mercy mean forgiving those who hurt us, giving them a second chance, and not taking revenge. Forgiving does not mean the hurt didn't matter; it means we choose to let go of anger and wish the other person good. God forgives us every time we are sorry, and Jesus forgave even from the cross. We pray, \"Forgive us our trespasses, as we forgive those who trespass against us.\"",
 "God forgives me, so I forgive.",
 ["Say 'I forgive you' when someone is sorry","Don't hit back when someone is unkind","Say sorry when you hurt someone","Give a sibling a second chance","Pray the Our Father slowly","Pray for someone who was unkind to you"],
 ["Let go of an old grudge","Forgive without bringing it up again","Ask forgiveness from someone you hurt","Choose not to get even","Make an examination of conscience","Plan to go to Confession soon"],
 ["How did we forgive each other this week?","Why does God want us to forgive?"],
 "Merciful Jesus, help me forgive others as You forgive me. Amen.",
 "Be kind and forgiving, just as God has forgiven you in Christ.", ["forgive","sorry","mercy","peace"]),
("Humility","Temperance","white","Philippians 2:3","In humility, let each esteem others better than themselves.","Phil 2:3",
 "Humility means not bragging or needing to be the center of attention. Every gift comes from God!",
 "Humility means not boasting, not always seeking the spotlight, and not thinking we are more special than others. A humble person knows that every talent is a gift from God and is happy to let others shine. Saint Paul says to think of others as more important than ourselves. Jesus, the Son of God, was humble: He was born in a stable and washed feet.",
 "My gifts come from God.",
 ["Let someone else go first","Clap for someone else's success","Don't brag about winning","Say thank you when you get help","Do a hidden good deed","Thank God for your talents"],
 ["Do a job no one will notice","Praise someone else's work sincerely","Ask for help when you need it","Accept correction without excuses","Serve without seeking thanks","Read about Mary's humble 'yes'"],
 ["When did we let someone else shine this week?","How did Jesus show humility?"],
 "Jesus, meek and humble of heart, make my heart like Yours. Amen.",
 "In humility, think of others as more important than yourself.", ["humble","gift","serve","quiet"]),
("Prudence (Virtue Challenge)","Temperance","white","Proverbs 14:15","The discreet man considereth his steps.","Prv 14:15",
 "Prudence means thinking carefully before you speak or act: Is this a good choice?",
 "Prudence means thinking carefully about whether a word or an action is a good choice before we say or do it. It means stopping, thinking, and choosing wisely. The Book of Proverbs says the wise person considers his steps. Prudence helps us avoid danger, choose good friends, and do what is right in each situation. The Holy Spirit helps us with good judgment.",
 "Stop, think, then choose.",
 ["Stop and think before you speak","Ask a parent before doing something new","Think: Is this safe?","Choose a good show or game","Think about how your words will feel","Ask the Holy Spirit to help you choose"],
 ["Think about consequences before acting","Wait a day before a big decision","Choose friends who help you be good","Ask a wise adult for advice","Plan your week so the important comes first","Pray before a hard choice"],
 ["What good choice did we think through this week?","How can we stop and think before we act?"],
 "Holy Spirit, help me think before I act and choose what is good. Amen.",
 "A wise person thinks carefully about each step.", ["think","choose","careful","wise"]),
("Self-Control","Temperance","white","Proverbs 16:32","He that ruleth his spirit, is better than he that taketh cities.","Prv 16:32",
 "Self-control means being the boss of your feelings and actions. You can wait, breathe, and choose!",
 "Self-control means guiding our feelings and actions and holding back impulses. When we feel angry, greedy, or impatient, we can stop, breathe, and choose what is right. Proverbs says the person who rules his own spirit is stronger than a soldier who captures a city! Self-control is a fruit of the Holy Spirit, and it grows each time we practice saying a good 'no.'",
 "I can stop, breathe, and choose.",
 ["Take three deep breaths when upset","Wait your turn without whining","Turn off the screen when asked","Save a treat for later","Use calm words when angry","Go to bed on time"],
 ["Give up a snack or game for a day","Count to ten before reacting","Do homework before playing","Keep your voice calm in an argument","Limit screen time and play outside","Offer a small sacrifice to Jesus"],
 ["When did we use self-control this week?","What helps us calm down when we are upset?"],
 "Holy Spirit, help me control my words, feelings, and actions. Amen.",
 "Ruling your own spirit is stronger than conquering a city.", ["calm","wait","control","breathe"]),
("Appreciation of Beauty","Transcendence","gold","Psalm 19:1","The heavens shew forth the glory of God.","Ps 19:1",
 "Appreciation of beauty means noticing and enjoying beautiful things. They point us to God!",
 "Appreciation of beauty means noticing and enjoying beauty and excellence everywhere: in nature, art, music, and in good people. A sunset, a song, a church window, or a kind act can fill us with wonder. The psalm says the heavens tell of the glory of God. All true beauty points us to God, who is Beauty itself.",
 "Beauty points me to God.",
 ["Look at the sky and thank God","Smell a flower or notice a tree","Listen to beautiful music","Look closely at a church window or statue","Notice something beautiful someone did","Draw the most beautiful thing you saw"],
 ["Take a walk and look for beauty","Look at a sacred painting together","Listen to a hymn or Gregorian chant","Praise someone's excellent work","Keep your room neat and beautiful","Watch a sunset or stars and pray"],
 ["What was the most beautiful thing we saw this week?","How does beauty help us think of God?"],
 "God of beauty, open my eyes to the wonders You made. Amen.",
 "The heavens tell of the glory of God!", ["beauty","wonder","art","nature"]),
("Gratitude","Transcendence","gold","Psalm 107:1","Give glory to the Lord, for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.","Ps 107:1",
 "Gratitude means noticing the good gifts in our lives and saying thank you to God and others.",
 "Gratitude means noticing the good things we have been given and feeling thankful. Everything good comes from God: our life, our family, food, friends, and faith. A grateful heart says thank you to God and to the people who help us, and it does not grumble. The word Eucharist means thanksgiving! At every Mass we thank God for His greatest gift, Jesus.",
 "Thank You, God, for You are good!",
 ["Thank God for your health when you wake","Thank the person who prepared your meal","Thank a friend who helped you today","Do your work gladly, without complaining","Thank God for something beautiful you see","Pray for your priest and catechist"],
 ["List three blessings before bed","Write a thank-you note to a teacher","Thank a parent for something they do daily","Go a whole day without complaining","Thank God for a hard thing that helped you","Say grace thoughtfully at every meal"],
 ["What is one thing our family was most grateful for this week?","Whom can we thank next week?"],
 "Thank You, Lord, for all Your gifts. Give me a grateful heart every day. Amen.",
 "Give thanks to the Lord, for He is good!", ["thanks","gift","grateful","bless"]),
("Hope (Virtue Challenge)","Transcendence","gold","Romans 15:13","Now the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing.","Rom 15:13",
 "Hope means expecting good things and working for them, trusting that God holds our future.",
 "Hope means expecting the best, working toward it, and trusting that a good future can be built with God. A hopeful person does not give up when things go wrong, because God is always at work. Saint Paul calls Him the God of hope, who fills us with joy and peace. Our greatest hope is heaven, where we will be with God forever.",
 "My hope is in God.",
 ["Say: 'God is with me' when things go wrong","Make a wish and pray about it","Cheer up someone who feels sad","Look forward to something good","Plant a seed and wait for it to grow","Pray for someone who needs hope"],
 ["Set a goal and take a first step","Find something good in a hard day","Encourage someone who is discouraged","Pray for people who are suffering","Remember a time God helped our family","Talk about heaven as a family"],
 ["What are we hoping for, and how can we work toward it?","When did God bring good out of a hard time?"],
 "God of hope, fill me with joy and peace. I trust my future to You. Amen.",
 "The God of hope fills us with joy and peace!", ["hope","trust","future","heaven"]),
("Humor","Transcendence","gold","Philippians 4:4","Rejoice in the Lord always; again, I say, rejoice.","Phil 4:4",
 "Humor means bringing smiles and seeing the bright side, with jokes that never hurt anyone.",
 "Humor means enjoying laughter, bringing smiles to others, and seeing the bright side of things. Good humor is playful and kind; it never makes fun of someone or hurts their feelings. Saints like Philip Neri and Thomas More loved to laugh. Saint Paul says to rejoice in the Lord always. Joy is a sign that we trust God, even on cloudy days.",
 "I rejoice in the Lord always!",
 ["Tell a kind joke at dinner","Make someone smile today","Laugh at your own small mistake","Find the bright side of a bad moment","Play a silly game with your family","Thank God for laughter"],
 ["Cheer up someone with kind humor","Never laugh at someone, only with them","Turn a grumpy moment into a smile","Learn about joyful Saint Philip Neri","Plan a family game or funny-story night","Say a joyful prayer of praise"],
 ["What made our family laugh together this week?","How can we tell if a joke is kind?"],
 "Lord, fill me with Your joy. Help me bring smiles that never hurt anyone. Amen.",
 "Rejoice in the Lord always! Joyful hearts bring smiles that never hurt.", ["joy","smile","laugh","rejoice"]),
("Spirituality","Transcendence","gold","Acts 17:28","For in him we live, and move, and are.","Acts 17:28",
 "Spirituality means living close to God every day. Our life has meaning because God made us and loves us.",
 "Spirituality means living by faith in God and knowing that our life has meaning and purpose in Him. As Catholics, we grow close to God through prayer, the Bible, the sacraments, and especially the Mass, where we receive Jesus. Saint Paul says that in God we live and move and have our being. God made each of us for a reason: to know Him, love Him, and serve Him.",
 "In God I live and move and am.",
 ["Make the Sign of the Cross when you wake","Say grace before every meal","Read a short Bible story together","Visit Jesus in a church","Say a night prayer with your family","Get ready for Sunday Mass"],
 ["Pray a decade of the Rosary as a family","Read and talk about Sunday's Gospel","Make a short visit to the Blessed Sacrament","Learn about your patron saint","Offer your day to God each morning","Go to Mass and pay close attention"],
 ["Where did we feel close to God this week?","How can we make prayer part of every day?"],
 "My God, I believe in You, I hope in You, and I love You. Help me live close to You. Amen.",
 "In God we live and move and have our being. He made me for a reason!", ["prayer","faith","God","Mass"]),
]
